{title: Shenandoah}
{artist: Traditional}
{key: G}

{c: Verse 1}
Oh [G]Shenan[C]doah, I [G]long to [Em]hear you,
A[G]way, you [C]rolling [D]river.
Oh [G]Shenan[C]doah, I [G]long to [Em]hear you,
A[G]way, I'm [D]bound a[G]way, 'cross the wide Mis[C]souri.

{c: Verse 2}
Oh [G]Shenan[C]doah, I [G]love your [Em]daughter,
A[G]way, you [C]rolling [D]river.
For [G]her I'd [C]cross your [G]roaming [Em]water,
A[G]way, I'm [D]bound a[G]way, 'cross the wide Mis[C]souri.
